---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
const components = [
  {name:"Kimi Delta Attention",tag:"HYBRID ATTENTION",idea:"Channel-wise forgetting and delta-rule updates; recurrent and chunkwise formulations, plus the optimized FLA GPU path.",code:"src/kimi_k3/attention/kda/",doc:"/docs/architecture/",test:"tests/equivalence/test_kda_chunkwise_vs_recurrent.py"},
  {name:"Gated MLA",tag:"ATTENTION",idea:"Low-rank KV representation, partial RoPE dimensions and an output gate, integrated alongside KDA in the decoder schedule.",code:"src/kimi_k3/attention/gated_mla.py",doc:"/docs/architecture/",test:"tests/unit/attention/test_gated_mla.py"},
  {name:"Attention Residuals",tag:"RESIDUAL PATH",idea:"Learned residual aggregation across local blocks, integrated at the attention and feedforward sublayers.",code:"src/kimi_k3/model.py",doc:"/docs/architecture/",test:"tests/integration/test_kimi_k3.py"},
  {name:"Stable LatentMoE",tag:"SPARSE FFN",idea:"Top-2 routed experts with shared experts, a latent bottleneck and Quantile Balancing in the training path.",code:"src/kimi_k3/moe/stable_latent_moe.py",doc:"/docs/architecture/",test:"tests/unit/moe/test_stable_latent_moe.py"}
];
---
<SiteLayout current="paper" title="Paper to Code — Kimi K3 from Scratch" description="How Kimi K3 architecture concepts are translated into readable PyTorch modules and tested implementations.">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="page-kicker">02 / ARCHITECTURE & IMPLEMENTATION</div>
    <h1>From paper <em>to code.</em></h1>
    <p>A map of the architecture and its implementation—not another mathematical tutorial. Each mechanism has an explicit path from the paper to readable PyTorch, numerical checks, and the implementation used for training.</p>
    <div class="journey" aria-label="Implementation methodology"><span>Paper</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>Derivation</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>PyTorch</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>Tests</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>Training</span></div>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="section-rail"><span class="section-index">01 / COMPONENTS</span><span class="rail-line"></span></div>
    <div class="section-main"><div class="section-topline">IMPLEMENTATION MAP</div><h2>Four building <em>blocks.</em></h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Explore each component, the decision it embodies, and the code that implements it. Detailed configuration and usage live in Docs; broader mathematical background can live in independent articles.</p>
      <div class="component-grid">
        {components.map((item, i) => <article class="component-card"><div class="component-number"><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,"0")}</span><span>{item.tag}</span></div><h3>{item.name}</h3><p>{item.idea}</p><div class="component-links"><a href={`https://github.com/adriaflores/kimi-k3-from-scratch/tree/main/${item.code}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source ↗</a><a href={`https://github.com/adriaflores/kimi-k3-from-scratch/blob/main/${item.test}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tests ↗</a><a href={item.doc}>Docs ↗</a></div></article>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section"><div class="section-rail"><span class="section-index">02 / VALIDATION</span><span class="rail-line"></span></div><div class="section-main"><div class="section-topline">FROM THEORY TO EVIDENCE</div><h2>Correctness is <em>measured.</em></h2><p class="section-lead">The readable reference path is not the whole production system. The project uses equivalence and integration tests to verify boundaries, gradients and behavior before optimized training.</p><div class="process-grid">
    <div class="process-card"><span>01 / REFERENCE</span><h3>Readable PyTorch</h3><p>Inspect core equations and model wiring without the complexity of GPU-specific kernels.</p></div>
    <div class="process-card"><span>02 / EQUIVALENCE</span><h3>Numerical checks</h3><p>Compare recurrent and chunkwise KDA; compare the fused GPU path with justified tolerances.</p></div>
    <div class="process-card"><span>03 / INTEGRATION</span><h3>Model assembly</h3><p>Exercise the mixed attention schedule, MoE, gradients and the full decoder stack.</p></div>
    <div class="process-card"><span>04 / SCALE</span><h3>Optimized execution</h3><p>The KDA GPU path uses the external FLA Triton implementation. We document that boundary explicitly.</p></div>
  </div><div class="section-next"><span>WHAT COMES AFTER IMPLEMENTING?</span><a class="text-link" href="/training/">Training: making it run at scale <span>↗</span></a></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
